{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgAFisp6CHCky842DHCVj","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The Recovery middleware now handles `http.ErrAbortHandler` quietly. Before this change it treated that panic like any other crash: it logged a full stack trace and called the recovery handler, which overwrote the status with a 500.\n\n- **Fix (`recovery.go`):** a panic whose value `errors.Is` `http.ErrAbortHandler` now takes the same path as a broken pipe. It logs one short line with no stack trace, records the error on the context, and aborts without writing a status.\n- **Test (`recovery_test.go`):** I added `TestPanicWithAbortHandler`. It panics with `http.ErrAbortHandler` after setting status 204, then checks that the status stays 204 and that no \"panic recovered\" trace is logged. It fails without the fix and passes with it (gate passed). I only ran the `TestPanicWith*` tests, not the full suite.\n- **One behaviour to know:** the middleware swallows the panic instead of re-panicking it. So when gin's Recovery is in use, `net/http` never sees the panic and won't cut the connection short the way it normally does for `ErrAbortHandler`."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1390,"cache_read_input_tokens":33853,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1390,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"cbab31a1-9535-4aca-ab96-7cf9bda596f0","uuid":"79fc6b81-71ea-4b9d-a2cd-6cd191728a90","timestamp":"2026-10-18T19:28:23.403Z","request_id":"req_011CgAFisbgWJN59PQGCMAVR"}
