ace, records the error on the context, and aborts without writing a status.\n- **Test (`recovery_test.go`):** I added `TestPanicWithAbortHandler`. It panics with `http.ErrAbortHandler` after setting status 204, then checks that the status stays 204 and that no \"panic recovered\" trace is logged. It fails without the fix and passes with it (gate passed). I only ran the `TestPanicWith*` tests, not the full suite.\n- **One behaviour to know:** the middleware swallows the panic instead of re-panicking it. So when gin's Recovery is in use, `net/http` never sees the panic and won't cut the connection short the way it normally does for `ErrAbortHandler`.","ttft_ms":2918,"type":"result","duration_ms":24344,"uuid":"19bad03c-6a86-4cef-bbe5-0e6491b49053","ttft_stream_ms":2206,"time_to_request_ms":134,"first_content_frame_ms":2206,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
